        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(android): localize native app surfaces",
        "body": "Related: #104979\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nAndroid exposed 21 app-language resources while onboarding, settings, chat, sessions, voice, notifications, accessibility, and background runtime surfaces still rendered user-facing literals in English.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds deterministic Android resources generated from the checked-in native translation artifacts, routes runtime and retained presentation copy through the selected app locale, and adds exact coverage checks for typed UI models, helper returns, interpolations, XML references, generated-resource parity, and raw Kotlin presentation strings. User content, gateway-provided labels, identifiers, commands, paths, URLs, and retained controller data remain verbatim.\n\nLocale ownership is explicit: Android framework locales are authoritative on API 33+, live AppCompat locales are authoritative on API 31-32, and AppCompat XML is read only for cold startup before a delegate attaches.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAndroid users selecting any of the 21 supported locales receive localized copy across the main app workflows, notifications, and background runtime surfaces. The build rejects new uncovered UI literals, stale generated locale resources, and dead resource references.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFinal reviewed SHA: `3b06d78ceccf85523553bad093bac8edcf3b4bd1`\n\n- Exact head: native inventory check passed with 3,780 entries and 21 locale artifacts; Android catalog check passed with 1,370 keys across 21 locales; `git diff --check` passed.\n- Scanner/tooling coverage: 30 focused tests passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxaxrwdexh43wdnwdp4wg2my`: `./gradlew ktlintCheck testPlayDebugUnitTest lintPlayDebug lintThirdPartyDebug assemblePlayDebug --no-daemon` passed; 1,315 unit tests passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxazph2ttytzvhczm6fbg770`: `pnpm check:changed` passed on runtime code SHA `4934ccba7867c591cf3701cf07d2f69c15016d51`.\n- Final commit `3b06d78ceccf85523553bad093bac8edcf3b4bd1` only removes the release-owned root changelog entry. An exact-head rerun reused a polluted Testbox checkout, expanded to all packages, and failed on unrelated root/package shrinkwrap drift; no Android lane failed.\n- Two fresh independent reviews found no remaining actionable issues.\n- Merge-tree against current `origin/main` is clean.\n\nResidual proof gap: no real-device API 31/33 end-to-end language-switch run; AndroidX source contracts and Robolectric coverage own this boundary.\n",
